column6:
•	The SPDA was created primarily to addresses the root causes of the Moro rebellion and to implement development interventions in Mindanao.
•	Its mission is to alleviate socio-economic challenges of individuals affected by armed conflict and other vulnerable sectors.
•	As a government-owned and controlled corporation the SPDA is tasked to continuously generating revenues to support its corporate social responsibilities.
•	In the year 2019, the SPDA has established a poultry farm located at Brgy. Labon, Sulop, Davao del Sur in partnership with the San Miguel Foods Corporation. The capacity of the farm is 80,000 heads per cycle.
•	The project aimed to increase broiler chicken production due to COVID-19’s impact.
•	The supply and demand disparity remains evident to this day, as evidenced by a higher retail price of chicken compared to the pre-pandemic era. 
•	The increasing Muslim population, particularly in Mindanao, has driven the persistent surge in demand for chicken meat. The 2020 Census of the Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA) recorded 6,981,710 Muslims, representing 6.4% of the country’s population. This figure has risen to 7.9 million in 2022, an 11.6% increase over the previous two years.

Why Halal?

•	To serve the domestic requirements of the rising Muslim population and other individuals with dietary restrictions;
•	To attract a larger Muslim tourists and enhances the country’s reputation as an investment and tourist destination;
•	Boosts the tourism industry;
•	Become a major player in the local halal market, especially for poultry and aquaculture industry;
•	It aligns with religious and economic goals, promoting cultural diversity and economic growth;
•	Fosters opportunities for international trade.
•	The Authority recognized the need for a reliable halal feed supply using halal-compliant raw materials to produce a globally acceptable halal poultry and aquaculture products.
